&lt;p&gt;Join &lt;a href="https://womeninenergy.energypolicy.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Women in Energy&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.pillsburylaw.com/en/" target="_blank"&gt;Pillsbury&lt;/a&gt; in Washington, DC, for a conversation examining the key trends and developments shaping the energy industry, where opportunities are emerging, and how professionals can position themselves for success across the sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The energy landscape is undergoing significant transformation. Rising electricity demand, the expansion of data centers and artificial intelligence, grid modernization, energy security priorities, evolving federal and state policies, and continued investment in nuclear, renewables, oil and gas, energy storage, and critical infrastructure are creating new challenges and opportunities. These developments are influencing how energy is produced, financed, regulated, delivered, and consumed&amp;mdash;and redefining the skills and perspectives organizations need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As companies respond to changing market conditions, technological advances, growing demand, and shifting policy priorities, employers are seeking a wide range of technical and non-technical expertise. This creates opportunities for professionals with traditional energy backgrounds as well as those bringing relevant experience from other industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The program will explore the trends and developments transforming the energy sector, where investment and business opportunities are emerging, and how these changes are creating new professional pathways. Speakers will discuss emerging technologies and business models, shifts in investment and demand, changes in the policy and regulatory environment, the roles and skills employers are seeking, and how transferable experience can translate across industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The conversation will also address the practical realities of navigating a dynamic energy market, including where to find opportunities, how to identify roles that align with your experience, and how professionals can adapt as industry priorities continue to evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The evening will conclude with a networking reception, giving attendees an opportunity to connect with energy professionals, employers, and others working across the sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you are an early-career professional, an established energy professional, a professional considering a transition, or returning to the workforce, this event will provide a broader understanding of where the energy industry is headed&amp;mdash;and how you can contribute to its future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brazil and the United States: Trade, Tariffs, and Defense Cooperation&lt;br /&gt;
