&lt;p&gt;Do you know when to use a bar graph instead of a line graph or a histogram instead of a scatterplot? Wouldn&amp;rsquo;t it be great if you could just add your files to a template and generate reports complete with data visualizations? If you ever wanted to automate your reporting or analysis, this workshop, the second part of An R Refresher, is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ll explore how to use Quarto, an open-source publishing system that lets you create dynamic documents, presentations, websites, and reports by combining text, code, and analysis in a single reproducible workflow. You&amp;rsquo;ll also learn when to use different data visualizations and how to create them. While the workshop will use R and the tidyverse, Quarto can also be used with Python.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an intermediate level workshop. There is no need to attend the first R Refresher but attendees should have experience with working with spreadsheets using R and should bring their laptop.&lt;/p&gt;

